      <section>
        <h2>What I work on</h2><p>
          I lead data platform work at a healthcare company. I build
          event-driven ingestion on AWS with Lambda, SQS and ECS, long-running
          services in Kotlin, and PostgreSQL/Supabase warehouses modeled with
          Kimball star schemas.
        </p><p>
          The common thread is replacing fragile manual data processes with
          automated systems that can be audited and recover from failure. In a
          healthcare setting, access control, audit logging and authentication
          are design constraints from the start.
        </p>
      </section><section>
        <h2>How I work with people</h2><p>
          When someone on my team hits a wall, I'd rather debug it with them and
          talk through the reasoning than hand over a fix. Understanding why
          something failed is part of making the next attempt better.
        </p>
      </section><section>
        <h2>Before this</h2><p>
          I earned a B.S. in Computer Science at the University of West Florida,
          with a concentration in Artificial Intelligence and Software
          Engineering.
        </p><p>
          Some of that work lives in the <a href="/projects/">project archive</a
          >: a compiler front end in C, a C++ Minesweeper, and an image
          classifier built with TensorFlow and Keras.
        </p>
      </section><section>
